post_install() {
    cat << 'EOF'
================================================================================
MMU VPN Tray - Post-Installation Setup
================================================================================
The package installed the following system files:

  /etc/openfortivpn/mmu-vpn.conf   OpenFortiVPN configuration
  /etc/sudoers.d/openfortivpn      Passwordless rules for openfortivpn,
                                   pkill and resolvectl

1. Sudoers Permissions:
   The sudoers rule applies to members of the 'wheel' group. Make sure your
   user is in that group:
     groups | grep -qw wheel || sudo usermod -aG wheel "$USER"
   (Log out and back in for the group change to take effect.)

   To allow a specific account instead, edit the file:
     sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/openfortivpn

   Verify the sudoers file:
     sudo visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/openfortivpn

2. Per-user Configuration (optional):
   The tray uses /etc/openfortivpn/mmu-vpn.conf by default. To override it
   for your user, copy it to your home directory:
     mkdir -p ~/.config/openfortivpn
     cp /etc/openfortivpn/mmu-vpn.conf ~/.config/openfortivpn/mmu-vpn.conf
     chmod 600 ~/.config/openfortivpn/mmu-vpn.conf
   ~/.config/openfortivpn/mmu-vpn.conf takes precedence when it exists.

3. Autostart in Hyprland (hyprlua):
   Add to your startup commands in ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua:
     hl.on("hyprland.start", function()
         hl.exec_cmd("mmu-vpn-tray")
     end)
================================================================================
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
